Third-party and derived material
--------------------------------

* firmware/fips202_lca.c and firmware/fips202.h are derived from the FIPS 202
  implementation in the PQClean project (https://github.com/PQClean/PQClean),
  itself based on the public-domain implementation in
  crypto_hash/keccakc512/simple/ from SUPERCOP (http://bench.cr.yp.to/supercop.html)
  by Ronny Van Keer, and the public-domain "TweetFips202" implementation by
  Gilles Van Assche, Daniel J. Bernstein, and Peter Schwabe. These portions are
  public domain (CC0-1.0).

* third_party/PQClean is a git submodule of the PQClean project
  (https://github.com/PQClean/PQClean). PQClean code is licensed per scheme,
  predominantly CC0-1.0 with some MIT and Apache-2.0 components; see the
  LICENSE files inside the submodule.

* third_party/picorv32 is a git submodule of YosysHQ PicoRV32
  (https://github.com/YosysHQ/picorv32), licensed under the ISC license; see
  the submodule's COPYING file.

* verification/vectors/external/cctv_mlkem768_ntt.json contains ML-KEM-768
  intermediate values extracted from the C2SP Community Cryptography Test
  Vectors project (https://github.com/C2SP/CCTV), published under CC0-1.0;
  the source file URL and its SHA-256 are recorded inside the JSON.

* The pinned Yosys runtime is installed from the @yowasp/yosys npm package
  (ISC-packaged distribution of Yosys, https://yosyshq.net/yosys/), used as a
  build/verification tool and not redistributed in this repository.
